.SH NAME
source \- execute commands in a shell script in the current shell
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B source
.I file
.SH DESCRIPTION
The shell reads commands from
.I file.
.B Source
commands can be nested; if they are nested too deeply, the shell can
run out of file descriptors.
.SH LIMITATIONS
An error in a
.B source
at any level terminates all nested
.B source
commands.
Input during 
.B source
commands is never placed on the history list. 
.B Source
output cannot be re-directed.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fIThe C Shell\fR in the ZEUS Utilities Manual

